---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-88-work-labor-livelihoods-economic-democracy-registry.json";

const access = registry.job_access_matching_hiring_nondiscrimination_dossiers;
const quality = registry.job_quality_wages_benefits_hours_safety_ledgers;
const voice = registry.worker_voice_organizing_collective_bargaining_economic_democracy_registers;
const livelihood = registry.livelihood_security_displacement_just_transition_long_horizon_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Work, Labor, Livelihoods And Economic Democracy | FTFN" description="Thirty-two inactive job-access, job-quality, worker-voice, economic-democracy, livelihood-security, displacement, and just-transition records.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-work-labor-livelihoods-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Work And Livelihoods</div><h1 class="page-title">A job posting is not an available job, and reemployment is not a just transition.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 88 traces whether real jobs are accessible; whether employment is safe, dignified, stable, and adequately compensated; whether workers can organize and bargain; and whether households and places remain secure through automation, climate, industrial change, and displacement.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive job-access dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive job-quality ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive worker-voice registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive livelihood ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 labor decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Job Access, Matching And Hiring</div><h2>Eight job-access dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/job-access-matching-hiring-001/">Read the job-access guide</a></div><div class="grid">{access.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.job_access_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/work-labor-livelihoods/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Actual vacancies, lawful standing, accessible recruitment, accommodations, fair matching, selection, explanation, appeal, start, retention, and independent review remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Job Quality, Wages, Benefits, Hours And Safety</div><h2>Eight job-quality ledgers contain no decent-work finding.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/job-quality-decent-work-001/">Read the decent-work guide</a></div><div class="grid">{quality.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.job_quality_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/work-labor-livelihoods/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.job_quality_wages_benefits_hours_safety_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Employment classification, pay, hours, benefits, health, safety, dignity, stability, workload, surveillance, grievance, accommodations, mobility, continuity, and review remain unassessed.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Worker Voice, Organizing And Economic Democracy</div><h2>Eight worker-voice registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/worker-voice-organizing-collective-bargaining-001/">Read the worker-voice guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{voice.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/work-labor-livelihoods/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.worker_voice_organizing_collective_bargaining_economic_democracy_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Association, union recognition, organizing access, retaliation protection, bargaining, agreements, grievance, enforcement, co-determination, cooperatives, employee ownership, remedies, and audit remain unassessed.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.worker_voice_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Livelihood Security, Displacement And Just Transition</div><h2>Eight livelihood ledgers contain no transition finding.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/automation-climate-industrial-transition-001/">Read the just-transition guide</a></div><div class="grid">{livelihood.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/work-labor-livelihoods/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.livelihood_security_displacement_just_transition_long_horizon_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Income and cost security, social insurance, care, savings, debt, layoff, automation, climate transition, retraining, reemployment quality, regional diversification, distribution, economic agency, and audit remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.livelihood_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty labor and livelihood state.</h2><p>The export publishes the complete control surface without treating a posting as a job, employment as decent work, a wage as household security, training as mobility, consultation as bargaining power, or reemployment as just transition—and without hiring, classifying, bargaining, scoring, ranking, or changing a stage.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/work-labor-livelihoods-economic-democracy.json">Work, labor, and livelihoods JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
